    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d552-a1">

                <pb facs="0557" n="1291" xml:id="pg1291"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 698.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herbert to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November 30,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith for
                    your information a copy of a letter from Rear-Admiral T. O. Selfridge,
                    commanding United States naval force on the European station, transmitting a
                    copy of one received from the commanding officer of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi>, reporting further particulars
                    concerning the affair at Adana, and the trial of the offenders.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. A. Herbert</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
